WEBVTT

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:10.650
The Faraway Paladin

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:36.000
I must also consider the 
option of killing you.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.410
How frightening.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.440
And how would you have me die?

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:45.100
I will say you were poisoned in 
the battle with the wyvern,

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:48.710
and that treatment came too late 
when you started to spit up blood.

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:51.210
<i>I understand what he's saying.</i>

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.530
<i>A hero who can't even prove his identity</i>

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:58.170
<i>is asking him for forces to operate 
in a region he doesn't even govern.</i>

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:00.630
<i>Of course he'd see it as dangerous.</i>

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:06.750
<i>I can handle those two, but there's 
still the risk of projectile weapons,</i>

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.610
<i>and the prince is pretty skilled himself.</i>

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.610
<i>No, it's pointless to think about it.</i>

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.930
<i>In any case, I have to get 
through this somehow.</i>

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:22.190
<i>I need to speak from the heart 
and plead my case earnestly.</i>

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.320
Your Highness...

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:25.500
What?

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.290
If all saltiness were to 
disappear from the world,

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.450
what would give salt its salty flavor?

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:38.230
If all those who carry a flame 
live only in the sunlight,

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:40.770
upon what do they shine their flames?

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:47.380
I have received a part of that flame 
from Gracefeel, the goddess of light.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:49.680
I believe the ones who carry that flame

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:53.460
are the ones who should march 
first into the darkness.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.700
They must shine the light upon 
those who lament in darkness,

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:59.290
and light the path for 
those who follow behind.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.780
So please, I beg of you.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:08.980
Can you somehow grant permission 
for this undertaking of mine?

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:17.960
William, this path will 
only lead to despair.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:22.710
It won't work, and even if it does, 
you will pay the price.

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:26.060
I have business with that 
despair you speak of.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:28.420
Oh? How so?

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:33.780
I don't like its face, so I want 
to kick it as hard as I can.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.530
Kick it in the face? I like that!

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:46.040
Come to think of it, you are 
a high priest, aren't you?

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:48.370
And you have quite a good friend, too.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.660
What, you didn't notice?

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:55.560
When I said I was going to kill you,

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:59.950
that half-elf there gave me 
quite the murderous glare.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.210
Wh-What're you talkin' about?

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:04.640
I was just steeling myself 'cause 
I figured you'd kill me, too.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.950
Damn it, don't look so happy!

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:08.510
Bishop, please stop!

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:10.870
His Highness is with a guest at the moment!

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:11.170
Please wait, Father!

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.710
Stay out of my way!

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:15.430
You damned fools!

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:21.190
Prince Ethelbald, do not act irrationally!

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:26.040
Oh? Whatever do you mean, Bishop Bagley?

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.650
Do not play dumb with me!

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:31.470
This young man is registered 
with my temple!

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:34.620
Though it may be temporary, 
he is a member of the temple!

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:37.260
And you beckon him here 
without a word to me?

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:40.110
Do you mean to disregard 
the temple's authority?!

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:42.430
Oh, I had no idea.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:44.160
Is this true?

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:45.520
Uh, yes.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:48.150
Ignorance is no excuse!

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:51.720
You cannot forego verification 
protocol simply because I was away!

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:56.700
So you say, but the people from your 
temple seemed happy to send him to me.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:59.100
Hmph! A total lack of discipline!

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.480
I will give them a stern talking-to later!

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:02.520
In any case, he—

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:05.150
The thing is, Bishop Bagley...

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:07.300
He is not what you think he is.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.410
Huh?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.610
He came here asking me to 
assemble a private army.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:14.970
Says he wants to save the 
poor people of Beast Woods.

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:15.990
What?!

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:17.990
Y-You—

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:22.760
I would be lying if I said it never 
crossed my mind to kill him right here.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.410
But he's just so frank.

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:28.090
Somehow, I started to 
find it quite amusing.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:29.990
Which is why...

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:34.900
I'm thinking of appointing him as a knight.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.930
Would your temple give him its blessing?

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:42.490
You know, a paladin.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:46.410
The temple and I will share the 
responsibility and the profits equally.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:48.230
What do you say?

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:49.650
What?!

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:53.340
He would, of course, 
fall under our joint authority.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:55.900
If it comes to it, you could always 
have him excommunicated.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:58.400
Th-Th-That is not the issue here!

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.160
The temple can attest to his character,

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:05.810
and as the Wyvern Killer, he should 
have no problems with the rest.

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:07.550
This is proceeding too quickly!

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:11.580
I will return to the temple and think it over! 
Is that acceptable?!

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:12.480
Yes.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:17.150
But it would make me truly happy 
to see this happen, Bagley.

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:19.940
I've taken a liking to this young man.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:22.620
Assuming I do become his patron,

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:24.620
spare me your silly games!

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:27.790
You, novice boy! We're leaving!

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:28.710
R-Right.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:38.660
Honestly, what a troublemaker.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:42.660
Demanding a private army? 
What were you thinking?

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:42.010
What's that old geezer's deal?

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:43.990
Uh, Menel, he's...

00:06:43.990 --> 00:06:46.330
Especially you, novice!

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.890
How dare you go and take matters 
into your own hands?!

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:52.680
So what if we did? 
It's not like you're our boss or anything.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.020
Excuse me?!

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:55.720
I am the head of the temple, 
in case you forgot!

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.370
So what? You wanna fight over it?

00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:00.750
How dare you speak to me 
that way?! Insolence!

00:06:58.700 --> 00:06:59.900
I'm sorry.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:03.180
My father has struggled with many unresolved 
issues of late, and it has him on edge.

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:04.450
And I'm saying it ain't your business. 
We don't work for you.

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:06.220
No, I apologize for my friend's behavior.

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:05.360
Excuse me?!

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.220
Just so you know...

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:09.690
Just so <i>you</i> know, you 
two came to <i>my</i> temple!

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:10.980
Anyway, um... So you're 
Bishop Bagley's daughter?

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:10.460
I'm saying—

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:13.150
<i>I'm</i> saying, don't create problems for me!

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:13.960
Yes, though not by blood.

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:13.940
Look, first of all—

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:14.910
<i>First</i> of all, you—

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:19.800
He was once in charge of a temple in the 
capital that had a large orphanage.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:17.950
Will you quit cutting me off?! 
I'm still talking!

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:19.650
What?! You—

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:22.920
And stop talking down to me! 
Who do you think you are?!

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:21.170
Ah, I see.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:25.640
When His Highness Ethelbald asked 
my father to relocate here,

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:23.380
I am—

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.290
The head of the temple, right?

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:26.990
I'm telling you, 
that's got nothing to do with us!

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:28.200
I came to this continent along 
with a dozen or so others.

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:27.830
If you—

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:29.230
Ugh, I can't deal with this!

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.380
So that's what happened.

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:31.810
Don't you interrupt me! I'm still speaking!

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:33.330
<i>He's in a position where he 
can throw his weight around,</i>

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:32.610
What?!

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:35.780
Have you no respect for your superiors?!

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:37.270
<i>he has connections everywhere, 
and he has loyal subordinates.</i>

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:38.450
And I keep telling you, that's got 
nothing to do with anything!

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:39.690
Bishop Bagley.

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.640
Thank you for your help.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:46.510
Your intervention with the 
crown prince saved us.

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:49.370
Hmph! I did nothing to 
warrant your gratitude!

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:53.780
I only defended the temple's authority 
from the crown prince's selfishness.

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:55.890
You only happened to be a part of that.

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.680
Besides, when he becomes 
amused by something,

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:00.590
he has a habit of doing unthinkable things.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:02.390
It's truly a problem.

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:04.710
But be that as it may,

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:07.500
I must respect his worldly authority.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:10.730
I will be taking his proposal 
into consideration.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:13.760
You will remain in the chapel 
after the evening prayer.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:16.070
All right, I understand.

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:18.460
Oh, but... um...

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:19.470
What?

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.990
What is the "evening prayer"?

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:25.910
You absolute fool!

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:31.330
You know the prayer by the names 
"vespers" and "compline"?

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:34.700
Those holy practices were 
revised 200 years ago.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:38.320
Did you serve your apprenticeship 
under one of such a long-lived race?

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:41.990
Uh... Yes, you could say that.

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:46.020
Hah! So you aren't entirely ignorant, then.

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:49.760
Anna, fetch some books on the 
revisions to the liturgy,

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:53.300
and find a suitable teacher 
for him, as well.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:54.210
Yes, Father.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:56.290
This boy is a novice,

00:08:56.290 --> 00:09:00.010
and on top of that, an ancient who's 
come here from 200 years in the past.

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:01.770
He'll take a lot of work.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:19.570
Greetings, Bishop.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:22.830
Wait here a moment.

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:23.650
Of course.

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:40.130
<i>His praying form looks almost 
frighteningly masterful.</i>

00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:44.330
<i>Other than Mary, 
I've never seen such an expert.</i>

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:51.150
Now, then...

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:52.420
Um...

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:53.590
What?

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:54.800
As head of the temple,

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:57.790
you have most certainly earned a high 
level of divine protection, yes?

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:01.410
<i>Equal to my own, if not even higher.</i>

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:05.810
The people of the temple told me 
that you don't use the blessing.

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:08.290
And when you pray, either you 
don't let anyone watch,

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:10.260
or you don't apply yourself 
fully when others are present.

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:11.540
Why is that?

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:14.180
Hah! Foolish novice!

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:16.880
What do you think the blessing is?

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:19.110
Divine protection bestowed by a god.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:23.120
Then why did a god bestow 
divine protection upon you?

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:25.850
To give you special treatment?

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:27.580
Not so, correct?

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:30.370
To act through you.

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:36.180
Understand? The god wishes to 
achieve something through you.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:39.810
And in order to live up 
to the gods' ideals,

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:43.240
we must constantly be in thought 
about how to use the blessing.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:46.980
To use it as a tool for one's own convenience 
does not contribute to the gods' glory.

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:48.370
It only detracts from it.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:51.890
Most of those dimwits fail 
to understand that,

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:54.490
which is why they will one 
day lose the blessing.

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:56.590
I am the head of the temple.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:59.290
This land is wild, and development 
on it has barely begun.

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:03.330
To secure funding and rights, 
I must yell and intimidate.

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:07.250
To lay the groundwork, 
I must do favors and use bribery.

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:12.060
If I were to use such a high 
blessing in these circumstances,

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:15.930
the people would question why a man 
like me received divine protection.

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:19.980
Now, youngster, 
do you think this would contribute

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:23.280
to the glory of Volt, my guardian deity?

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.290
No.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:25.420
Precisely.

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:29.840
The correct course of action for blessings 
and prayers is to store them inside.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:36.080
I have entrusted the vice bishop with the 
glorification of the gods through blessings.

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.040
He is a very capable man,

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:41.540
skilled at winning the hearts of the 
people to the extent it is needed.

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:45.100
I can trust him with the bothersome, 
stressful role of being the face of the temple.

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:49.220
<i>Bishop Bagley really is talented.</i>

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:53.210
<i>He's rude, and he looks like a greedy 
monk who's always complaining,</i>

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:54.540
<i>but he's an amazing man.</i>

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.800
And what about you?

00:11:57.480 --> 00:12:02.340
Making a youngster who has yet to fully 
comprehend what the blessing is into a paladin?

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:06.240
The crown prince does so love his jokes!

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:07.900
Listen.

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:12.450
Don't do it. Nothing good will come 
of a novice attempting this.

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:15.190
I'll go to him and refuse 
for you, if you want.

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:19.180
Even the crown prince will surely 
give up if I give a firm rejection.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:19.960
What say you?

00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:25.010
Regardless, my goddess still wishes 
to achieve something through me.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:27.730
You will not change your mind?

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:29.590
I will not.

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.860
You are a fool.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:33.270
I agree.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:36.220
What did you swear to the goddess of flux?

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:40.740
To offer her my life, banish evil, 
and save the suffering.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:44.910
Rejoice!

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:50.130
You are the most dimwitted of all 
the dimwits I have seen here!

00:12:50.780 --> 00:12:55.540
I will send a few with you. 
The rest is up to you.

00:12:56.520 --> 00:12:57.970
Thank you.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:03.380
<i>I should respect this man, 
no matter what anyone else says.</i>

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:06.780
Let's go!

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:07.820
Welcome!

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:09.300
You're really putting those 
drinks away, mister!

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:16.230
Don't go for people who use 
adventuring as a job.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:20.180
Find people who seek adventure, for 
the glory and prestige of it.

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:23.470
Yeah. We need real ruffians 
who'll put their lives

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:25.980
on the line for battle and adventure.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:29.050
<i>Right, just like Blood.</i>

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:32.390
Demon beast horns... and demon beast hide?

00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:34.520
Those are their battle spoils.

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:37.000
It's the easiest way to 
show off their strength.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:38.570
C'mon, let's go.

00:13:43.350 --> 00:13:46.890
A chestnut-haired boy with a 
silver-haired elf-mix buddy...

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:48.110
There's no doubt.

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:50.420
He's been through a whole lot of training.

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:53.550
Hey, what's the famous Wyvern Killer

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:56.160
doin' in some pub in the middle of nowhere?

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:57.680
I'm looking for help.

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:00.340
Exploring Beast Woods?

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:03.140
Low pay... Your reward is glory and praise,

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:04.800
and there's no guarantee you'll survive?!

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:06.470
We're doin' this for a living, y'know!

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:08.700
We're not takin' a quest 
like this! Right, guys?

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:11.400
Yeah! Don't be so stingy!

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:17.780
Shut up, you blowhards.

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:29.810
When you see a swordsman, 
look at his fingers.

00:14:29.810 --> 00:14:34.140
You can tell by looking at his hands 
whether he'll allow any thoughts

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:36.650
that prevent him from drawing his weapon.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:41.870
Looks to me like what you want 
is a madman. Am I right?

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:44.730
Not a bunch of blowhards with 
good manners but no skills,

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:49.920
who've picked up the etiquette 
and patience to do any job,

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:52.540
but a bunch of shitheads who 
know no fear or manners.

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:55.120
The worst kind of scumball adventurers

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:57.530
who'll risk their lives for 
the dumbest ideals, right?

00:14:57.800 --> 00:15:00.170
That's why we've come here.

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:03.880
Hey, you hear that? Just like I said!

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:05.790
Tch! Bunch of damn lunatics!

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:07.940
You oughta buy our drinks for a change!

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:09.170
Yeah, that's right!

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:14.230
What're you hoping to get out 
of exploring Beast Woods?

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:16.470
Where we goin'? Ruins? Outdoors?

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.750
We don't bother with small fry!

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:20.220
The demon boss.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:28.150
The leader of the demons running rampant 
in the western part of Beast Woods,

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:31.560
whose subordinate demons are 
thought to command demon beasts.

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:33.050
That's a big fish.

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:33.870
Yes.

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:38.010
The location is unclear. 
Just finding him will be hell.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:41.840
We're talkin' instant death if 
we're ambushed during the search.

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:43.830
Most likely.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:45.470
In other words,

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:49.080
this is gonna be a nice, fun, 
stupid little jaunt.

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:57.080
Let me in on it.

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:59.170
All I need is food and a bed.

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:01.410
Even better if I make a 
little pocket change.

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:02.110
Me, too!

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:02.740
And me!

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:03.480
Leave it to us!

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:03.560
I'm in!

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:04.880
Of course, I'll have those for you!

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:10.880
I'm William G. Maryblood.

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:14.040
I'm Reystov.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.560
Whence cometh this disciple

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:26.590
to the lost goddess of 
flux, goddess of light?

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:31.490
The Disciple of the Light, the Wyvern Killer, 
the Peerless Powerhouse...

00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:30.540
<i>It's almost time for the ceremony.</i>

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:33.780
<i>I heard they wanted to make this a 
happy event to give work to people</i>

00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:36.010
The Faraway Paladin, William G. Maryblood.

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:36.560
<i>who lost their homes and jobs 
in the wyvern attack, but...</i>

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:41.300
Know the name of the new hero who has 
appeared in the city of white sails!

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:44.540
Hmm... I guess that should do it.

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:48.410
Bee, could you not write an epic 
about me right in front of me?

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:50.310
What? Why not?!

00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:53.930
You actually did do all that. 
What did you expect?

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:58.030
Look forward to hearing it! 
I'm gonna make it awesome!

00:16:59.130 --> 00:17:00.030
Hmm...

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:05.640
This many cows and horses will 
indeed come at a hefty price.

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:07.410
Oh, about that...

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:12.550
Can you negotiate to get us the sick 
and injured ones at a lower price?

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:13.430
What?

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:16.020
And then I'll heal all of them.

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:17.340
Oh... That makes sense.

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:21.690
Also, it would be a big help 
if you could start trade

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:24.630
between Beast Woods and Whitesails.

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:25.740
Hmm...

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:28.610
How much do you need me to 
give you to fund that?

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:32.940
Will, why don't you and I
have a serious business chat?

00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:34.880
Now, then...

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:36.790
G-Go easy on me...

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:38.340
I say go for it.

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:41.000
You need to have a good understanding 
of how money works.

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:41.870
Right.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:45.160
You're gonna be negotiating with 
Reystov and those other guys next.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:46.550
Reystov?!

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:49.340
Reystov the Penetrator is here?!

00:17:49.340 --> 00:17:50.620
Y-Yes, he is...

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:53.390
That's perfect! Let me interview him!

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:54.230
Huh?

00:17:55.580 --> 00:17:59.440
Making a habit of flaunting your own 
accomplishments leads to arrogance.

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:01.840
And arrogance dulls one's blade?

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:03.060
Exactly.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.260
That again?!

00:18:04.610 --> 00:18:06.780
This is why you're so useless!

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:08.390
I can't get any good ideas out of you!

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:12.030
So you two know each other?

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:14.370
We've talked a few times.

00:18:14.370 --> 00:18:16.700
No matter how many times I interview 
you, it's always the same!

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:18.370
I thought it'd be different this time!

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:20.560
You're just a stubborn, broody guy!

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:22.570
The answers don't change, 
no matter how many times you ask.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:26.410
All of your tales of heroism 
are so ambiguous!

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:29.940
I was gonna make something that came 
a little closer to the truth!

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:31.780
I can't believe how mean you're being!

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:34.620
Isn't reputation important 
to an adventurer?!

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:37.540
Whether it's to make a living 
or get ahead in life!

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:40.760
As long as you've got skills, 
those things come naturally.

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:46.020
I know you realize that even people with 
skills can be ruined by a bad reputation!

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:49.590
Even a warrior never knows what's 
going to be his downfall!

00:18:49.590 --> 00:18:50.850
Don't you agree, Will?

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:51.820
Uh...

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:55.690
A lot of Reystov's tales 
of heroism are ambiguous?

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:56.890
Yeah, exactly!

00:18:56.890 --> 00:19:00.130
This guy will accept a job 
to take down a huge threat,

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:03.710
then he just wanders off, kills it with 
one fatal stab, and wanders back!

00:19:03.710 --> 00:19:05.860
He hardly ever works with anyone else,

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:09.460
and he works so fast, hardly anyone 
knows what actually happened!

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:11.260
And he takes such a broad range of jobs!

00:19:11.260 --> 00:19:13.220
So the stories end up more 
and more embellished?

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:14.000
Yep!

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:17.880
I try to interview people, but all they 
do is fill in the gaps however they can!

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:21.110
I do embellish them a little bit,

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:24.010
but I like to add a little 
more truth to my tales!

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:25.010
No need.

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:26.480
That's what I'm talking about!

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:29.900
If only I had a little more to work with...

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:33.190
I know!

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:35.400
How about the Penetrator 
versus the Paladin?

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:38.410
Huh?! That sorta came out of nowhere...

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:41.180
You're putting Reystov on 
the spot, too! Right?

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:46.040
If I receive a challenge from a 
strong opponent, I have no choice.

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:47.530
Reystov?!

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:49.700
See?! You heard him!

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:54.220
Well, maybe when we're 
done in Beast Woods...

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:55.200
Yay!

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:56.600
That's a promise!

00:19:56.600 --> 00:19:58.180
This is great!

00:19:58.180 --> 00:20:02.440
I'll make this into a song that'll be sung for 
centuries, millennia—until the end of time!

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:28.580
I, Prince Southmark,

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:32.660
Ethelbald Rex Southmark, 
hereby declare you a knight.

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:39.170
May you become the protector of 
your temple, of those in need,

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:42.270
and of all those who 
believe in the virtuous gods,

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:46.210
who defy the evil gods and their violence.

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:09.330
You who strive to become a knight...

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:12.200
Uphold the teachings of the virtuous gods,

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:19.000
and protect all who suffer along 
with all who work through prayer.

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:54.080
I pray to my guardian deity, 
Enlight, the god of knowledge,

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:58.070
to serve as the intermediary to 
this young man's guardian deity.

00:21:58.070 --> 00:22:04.560
May Gracefeel, the goddess of light, forever shower this young man with her grace.

00:22:04.560 --> 00:22:10.540
Uphold your oath steadfastly, honor the 
teachings, and protect the weak.

00:22:10.730 --> 00:22:12.630
Be the light of the world!

00:22:12.900 --> 00:22:14.880
Be the light of the world!

00:22:14.880 --> 00:22:18.440
We celebrate the birth of a new knight!

00:22:17.560 --> 00:22:24.690
Episode 10 
Renowned Glory

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:20.900
Bring light to the farthest 
reaches of the earth!

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:23.190
Long live the paladin!

00:22:31.860 --> 00:22:33.190
Vice Bishop.

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:35.790
Thank you for blessing me.

00:22:35.790 --> 00:22:38.120
Think nothing of it.

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:41.920
It was an honor to receive such an 
important duty from the bishop.

00:22:41.920 --> 00:22:45.210
Ordinarily, this would be his job, but...

00:22:45.210 --> 00:22:49.980
I asked him, and he said he finds it 
bothersome to show people his pious side.

00:22:49.980 --> 00:22:51.300
It's too bad.

00:22:51.300 --> 00:22:52.630
I agree.

00:22:52.630 --> 00:22:55.590
For a man of his caliber to be 
so unknown to the public...

00:22:55.590 --> 00:22:57.440
So this is where you were!

00:22:57.440 --> 00:23:00.150
We're having grappling matches over there!

00:23:00.150 --> 00:23:01.930
Come join us for a round!

00:23:01.930 --> 00:23:03.050
Uh, okay...

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:04.860
Come with us, Menel!

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:05.940
No way.

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:08.840
Hey, it's the paladin's servant!

00:23:09.060 --> 00:23:11.370
Not my servant. He's my friend.

00:23:11.370 --> 00:23:12.550
I'm not your friend!

00:23:12.550 --> 00:23:13.250
Huh?!

00:23:13.250 --> 00:23:14.700
Will!

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:16.660
We're making a fortune!

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:18.430
And it's all thanks to your song!

00:23:20.890 --> 00:23:23.760
<i>Goddess, are you watching?</i>

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:26.510
<i>I'm getting by somehow. 
And I'll continue to.</i>

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:33.210
<i>And that's how I became 
the Faraway Paladin.</i>

00:23:35.600 --> 00:23:39.930
Episode 11
Valley of Despair
